  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 1200 AM CDT Tue Aug 11 2026\n\nThe upper ridge eventually will try to establish itself over the \nGulf leading to southerly to at times southwesterly flow aloft \nwhich should help to mitigate \"feels like\" temperatures somewhat. \nThat isn't to say that our actual air temperatures wont be hot, \nthey will, with most expected to see highs in the 99-103 degree \nrange. However the humidity due to the air coming off of Mexico \nand West TX will likely be drier. Highs will continue to remain in\nthe upper 90s to near 103 degree range for many areas each day \nduring this period. These higher temperatures combined with \nslightly higher humidity as a plume of tropical moisture looks to \nmove over the area by Friday at the earliest should result in \n\"feels like\" temperatures eclipsing 108 degrees for many. This \nwould likely be for areas mainly east of I-37/I-35. The hot and \nmainly dry weather looks to stick around heading into this weekend\nand additional heat advisories may be needed. Humidity values \nshould be a touch lower by the second half of the weekend. \nAdditionally, high temps mainly in the upper 90s to near 100 \nshould be expected as the ridge refocuses from the Gulf to the \nlower Mississippi Valley so we should stay just shy of heat \nadvisory criteria during this stretch. However it will still \ncontinue to be quite hot across the area so continue to check back\nfor updates and remember to practice safe heat safety.",
